        <mxCell id="notes" value="MAPPING AND CONSTRAINTS&lt;br/&gt;1:N mapping: parent PK becomes a foreign key in the child relation.&lt;br/&gt;Optional 1:1 extensions: FEEDBACK.complaint_id and COMPLAINT_EMBEDDING.complaint_id are NOT NULL + UNIQUE foreign keys to COMPLAINT.complaint_id.&lt;br/&gt;Alternate keys: ROLE(role_name), USER(email), DEPARTMENT(department_name), CATEGORY(department_id, category_name). Only primary keys are underlined here.&lt;br/&gt;All FKs are NOT NULL. Optional attributes: COMPLAINT.resolved_at; ASSIGNMENT.ended_at; STATUS_HISTORY.old_status and remarks; FEEDBACK.comment.&lt;br/&gt;Domains: priority ∈ {LOW, MEDIUM, HIGH, URGENT}; status ∈ {SUBMITTED, ASSIGNED, IN_PROGRESS, RESOLVED, REJECTED}; rating ∈ [1,5]; target_hours &amp;gt; 0.&lt;br/&gt;At most one active assignment: unique index on ASSIGNMENT(complaint_id) WHERE ended_at IS NULL. Preserve ended assignments.&lt;br/&gt;resolved_at is present iff status = RESOLVED; resolved_at ≥ created_at. ended_at ≥ assigned_at when present.&lt;br/&gt;Semantic rules require transactions / triggers: role checks, valid status transitions, current status / history consistency, feedback by reporter after resolution.&lt;br/&gt;pgvector: embedding VECTOR(384), fixed 384-dimensional model, cosine retrieval. content_hash detects stale complaint embeddings.&lt;br/&gt;Department is derived through COMPLAINT → CATEGORY → DEPARTMENT; no duplicate department_id in COMPLAINT.&lt;br/&gt;SQL implementation: quote logical identifiers consistently, e.g. public.&amp;quot;USER&amp;quot;, or map them to safe physical identifiers such as app_user." style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=17;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#222222;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;fontSize=19;fillColor=#f5f5f5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="70" y="1930" width="2680" height="450" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>